Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if the Sun never set?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.33,0:00:05.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You stand on a beach at noon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.33,0:00:07.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The light never fades.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.16,0:00:08.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No sunset.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.29,0:00:09.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No stars.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.51,0:00:11.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.32,0:00:12.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.04,0:00:14.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.44,0:00:17.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The ground never gets a chance to cool down.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.20,0:00:19.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Heat keeps building up.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.74,0:00:21.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one week.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.05,0:00:22.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You can't sleep properly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.58,0:00:24.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Your inner clock breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.44,0:00:27.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Crops wilt in the fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.51,0:00:28.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one month.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.86,0:00:30.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The oceans keep warming.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.53,0:00:33.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Monster storms start to form.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.06,0:00:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Rivers and lakes shrink.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.63,0:00:37.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.06,0:00:39.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Deserts spread across the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.32,0:00:42.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Night animals have nowhere left to hide.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.75,0:00:44.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.48,0:00:47.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Some people already live with a Sun that never sets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.87,0:00:52.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In Svalbard, Norway, it stays up for about four months every summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.54,0:00:54.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And it's still cold there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.24,0:00:57.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The Sun just stays low in the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.67,0:00:58.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.81,0:01:00.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Night isn't just darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.60,0:01:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It's how Earth cools down.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.63,0:01:04.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you miss the stars?
